  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A monoatomic gas performs a work of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>Q</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math> where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math> is the heat supplied to it. The molar heat capacity of the gas will be _____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> during this transformation.</p><p>Where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> is the gas constant.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "2",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Using first law of thermodynamics,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>W</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#916;</mi><mi>U</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>Q</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#916;</mi><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>n</mi><mi>R</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#916;</mi><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Therefore, molar heat capacity,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi></math></p>",
